dies in sub-Saharan Africa have reported better economic returns for conservation agriculture than for traditional practices. Even when similar or higher yields are obtained, there can be significant savings in labor and time. For example, a three-year study of twenty-four farms in Malawi found that conservation agriculture plots with intercropped maize and pigeon peas ( _Cajan"}
